// lexdb over TNS: the audit's wrong answers and wrong errors in the Oracle door (design/lexdb-new-features.md: O5 a table value
// constructor's column names as written and ORA-00931 / ORA-63814 without them, a CTE's column list's names; O8 GROUP BY's
// position (a constant, ORA-03162, unless ALTER SESSION SET group_by_position_enabled = TRUE) and HAVING's select alias; O15
// TRUNC of a TIMESTAMP is a DATE (the CREATE TABLE ... AS's column); O16 SUM and AVG of intervals; O28 UTL_ENCODE.BASE64_ENCODE and
// BASE64_DECODE (RAW in, RAW out) with UTL_RAW.CAST_TO_RAW and CAST_TO_VARCHAR2; a number running into _ (ORA-00911); an unknown
// function refused when bound, an empty input too (ORA-00904)), checked against Oracle Database Free 23.26 (gen_oracle.py --check:
// the answers below are Oracle's). Each statement runs with set lexdb_batch = off (the row engine) and on: "same" and the
// answer, or DIFFERENT and both.
